Do not treat every finalized object as a usertype in class_gc_event.

class_gc_event is tolua's __gc.  It opens by dereferencing
lua_touserdata(L,1) without checking what it was handed, which was safe
while only userdata had finalizers.  Since Lua 5.2 an object is marked for
finalization when it is given a metatable that already carries __gc -- and
tolua_classevents puts __gc on every class metatable, which
tolua_beginmodule then installs on the class *table*.  Those tables are
finalized too, at the latest when the state is closed, and for a table
lua_touserdata returns NULL, so the dereference is a null read.

The symptom is a segfault in lua_close after a binding has otherwise run
perfectly: every assertion passes, the script prints, and the process dies
on the way out.

Upstream: not submitted (project unmaintained since 2012); the AUR
          tolua++_5.3 package carries an equivalent guard
Applies-to: all environments
---
diff --git a/src/lib/tolua_event.c b/src/lib/tolua_event.c
index 210dfee..2cf0b82 100644
--- a/src/lib/tolua_event.c
+++ b/src/lib/tolua_event.c
@@ -432,8 +432,18 @@ static int class_gc_event (lua_State* L)
 */
 TOLUA_API int class_gc_event (lua_State* L)
 {
-	void* u = *((void**)lua_touserdata(L,1));
+	void* u;
 	int top;
+	/* Since Lua 5.2 an object is marked for finalization when it is given a
+	** metatable that already has a __gc field, and that catches more than the
+	** userdata this was written for: tolua_classevents puts __gc on every class
+	** metatable, and tolua_beginmodule then hands that metatable to the class
+	** *table*.  Those tables are finalized too -- at the latest when the state
+	** is closed -- and for a table lua_touserdata returns NULL, so
+	** dereferencing it below segfaults. */
+	if (lua_type(L,1) != LUA_TUSERDATA)
+		return 0;
+	u = *((void**)lua_touserdata(L,1));
 	/*fprintf(stderr, "collecting: looking at %p\n", u);*/
 	/*
 	lua_pushstring(L,"tolua_gc");
